{
  "description": "Ten compact interaction/reveal cues plus a quiet instrumental Pok\u00e9mon anime BGM loop. Existing seven polished cues remain; suspense, slam and a tighter ball release support the special-card charge-and-impact sequence.",
  "sourcePolicy": "Original seven cues plus suspense/slam use Kenney CC0 source samples. Ball release and the actual anime soundtrack use community-hosted Pok\u00e9mon audio under the user's stated license, with source uncertainty recorded individually. No oscillator beeps or generic replacement music.",
  "reproduce": "Run python3 scripts/polish-audio.py then python3 scripts/extend-cinematic-audio.py. Requires Python 3, curl, ffmpeg and ffprobe; optional REVEAL_AUDIO_SOURCE_CACHE, ASSET_FFMPEG, ASSET_FFPROBE. Missing files download from recorded public URLs; music source SHA-256 is pinned.",
  "encoder": "ffmpeg version 8.1.2 Copyright (c) 2000-2026 the FFmpeg developers",
  "formats": "Stereo MP3 at 192 kbps / 44.1 kHz, and OGG Opus at 128 kbps / 48 kHz. Container durations may include codec delay; decodedDuration is the audible buffer length.",
  "verification": "All 22 MP3/OGG files decode with ffmpeg -xerror, finite PCM and decoded durations within 3 ms. Ten effect pairs have oversampled peaks near -6 dBFS and clean tails. Music pair peaks near -12 dBFS and preserves a continuous loop boundary; all output SHA-256 hashes recorded.",
  "limitations": "Automated decode/timing/headroom checks are complete; no human listening review is claimed. Source and musical-seam limitations for the community Pok\u00e9mon music/effect are recorded in their entries. Lossy bytes may vary between encoder versions.",
